<p>Five countries — Spain, Ireland, the Netherlands, Slovenia and Iceland — are not taking part in the 2026 Eurovision Song Contest in Vienna because Israel remains in the competition during the war in Gaza, according to accounts of the withdrawals and boycott calls. The European Broadcasting Union allowed Israel to compete, and Israeli singer Noam Bettan qualified for Saturday’s final after performing “Michelle” in the first semifinal. Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez defended the withdrawal on Friday, saying it was consistent with Spain’s human-rights and international-law commitments and put Spain “on the right side of history”. Saturday’s final will feature 25 countries in the contest’s 70th edition. Protests in Vienna have targeted Israel’s participation, including an alternative “song protest” and a planned final-day march under the slogan “No Stage for Genocide”. During Bettan’s semifinal appearance, some audience members booed and chanted “Stop the Genocide,” while security removed four people from the arena, according to the Jewish Telegraphic Agency.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/tnyh__1wRhnMUdeezzNg2mZadnrkdzciHEE4jwN63KWmldEZHQiwaIJ0H-QtVNKI_TE2-EXfcq58m7oG4q36PQHxa--7sEiiFoUxpBvVVDBTGKyO6uHtTy3mtH5j9ULyX-_O8S3Y9106lxwRftrKzpnHTNMGuap6vsjHptxwRasaCERvgp5h7d-p_gIpiwQenhLaQmdiABKj73dqSJvBtapT_1HOXSAD5WWv4hY' alt='Noam Bettan, Israel&#x27;s representative at the 2026 Eurovision Song Contest, performs the song &#x27;Michelle&#x27; during the contest&#x27;s first semifinal.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Audience scale: Eurovision is billed as the world’s biggest live televised music event and typically reaches more than 150 million viewers.</li><li>Host entry: Austria’s entry in Vienna is Cosmó. The finalists are competing to succeed 2025 winner JJ and “Wasted Love”.</li><li>Artist appeal: More than 1,000 artists signed a call to boycott the show because Israel was allowed to participate.</li><li>Voting scrutiny: El País reported that this edition has drawn scrutiny over withdrawals and suspicions of televoting manipulation.</li></ul><blockquote>In the face of illegal war and also genocide, silence is not an option. And we cannot remain indifferent to what continues to happen in Gaza and Lebanon - Pedro Sánchez</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>European Broadcasting Union: Eurovision director Martin Green wrote in an email that organizers were preparing for all scenarios in response to the withdrawals. (<a href='https://www.expressen.se/noje/musik/landerna-som-bojkottar-eurovision-song-contest-ebus-svar/'>Expressen</a>)</li><li>Noam Bettan: Bettan said the initial reaction during his semifinal quickly gave way, in his view, to support from Israelis and non-Israelis in the arena and online. (<a href='https://www.jta.org/2026/05/14/israel/noam-bettan-says-he-is-tuning-out-stop-the-genocide-chants-as-he-heads-into-eurovision-final'>Jewish Telegraphic Agency</a>)</li><li>Austrian Young Greens: The youth wing affiliated with Austria’s Greens posted a video welcoming Bettan and argued that boycotting Israel, booing or harassing Israeli artists would not free Palestine and would make Jewish life in Europe less safe. (<a href='https://www.jta.org/2026/05/15/global/amid-eurovision-tensions-israelis-find-allies-in-austrias-youth-green-party-and-a-cafe'>Jewish Telegraphic Agency</a>)</li><li>Host-country foreign minister Beate Meinl-Reisinger: Meinl-Reisinger tried to dissuade boycott supporters by saying Eurovision was “not a tool for imposing sanctions,” according to El País. (<a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-05-15/why-eurovision-may-become-irrelevant-again.html'>El País</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c0e2g5y9wyeo'>Why is Ireland not taking part in this year&#x27;s Eurovision?</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/05/15/2026/five-european-nations-contest-israels-participation-in-eurovision'>Five European 